<p>You can print a document with crop marks applied.</p>
<p>This function is useful to print a document that has edges you want 
 to trim off.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<h2>What are Crop Marks?</h2>
<p>Crop marks are line markings for trimming documents.</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Crop marks are printed on front sides when 2 sided 
 printing is applied.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Output Settings</span> 
 menu of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Print Crop Marks</span> 
 check box.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span>.<br/>
 The <span class="Term-Soft">Print Crop Marks Details</span> dialog box 
 appears.</p></li>
<li><p>Specify the length of the crop marks in <span class="Term-Soft">Length of Crop Marks:</span>.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Select the 
 <span class="Term-Soft">First Page Only</span> when printing crop marks 
 on the first page only.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="6">
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
